-- Paragraph (a)(1) governs the certificate, and any other instrument filed before the initial board is
-- elected when the certificate did not name the initial directors. Paragraph (a)(2) governs "all other
-- instruments".
-- src:81 | (1) The certificate of incorporation, and any other instrument to be filed before the election of the initial board of directors if the initial directors were not named in the certificate of incorporation, shall be signed by the incorporator or incorporators (or, in the case of any such other instrument, such incorporator’s or incorporators’ successors and assigns). If any incorporator …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(a)(1) (src:81)
GIVEN i IS A `s 103(a) Instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(a)(1) the instrument is one that the incorporators sign` i MEANS
        i's `the instrument is the certificate of incorporation`
     OR (    i's `the instrument is to be filed before the election of the initial board of directors`
         AND (NOT (i's `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation`)))

-- The certificate must be signed by the incorporator or incorporators. Any other instrument of this kind may
-- also be signed by their successors and assigns, or, if an incorporator is not available, by the person
-- for whom the incorporator acted, if the instrument states the three things the text lists.
-- src:81 | (1) The certificate of incorporation, and any other instrument to be filed before the election of the initial board of directors if the initial directors were not named in the certificate of incorporation, shall be signed by the incorporator or incorporators (or, in the case of any such other instrument, such incorporator’s or incorporators’ successors and assigns). If any incorporator …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(a)(1) (src:81)
GIVEN i IS A `s 103(a) Instrument`
      s IS A `s 103(a)(1) Signing by the incorporators`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(a)(1) the instrument is signed as required of the incorporators` i s MEANS
    IF i's `the instrument is the certificate of incorporation`
    THEN s's `every incorporator signed`
    ELSE    s's `every incorporator signed`
         OR s's `the successors and assigns of the incorporators signed`
         OR (    s's `an incorporator is not available`
             AND s's `a person for whom or on whose behalf the incorporator acted as employee or agent signed`
             AND s's `the instrument states that the incorporator is not available and the reason`
             AND s's `the instrument states that the incorporator in executing the certificate acted as employee or agent for or on behalf of that person`
             AND s's `the instrument states that that person's signature is otherwise authorized and not wrongful`)

-- Paragraph (a)(2): the four alternatives a. to d.; b. and c. apply only if it appears from the instrument
-- that there are no officers (b.), or no officers or directors (c.). Alternative d. is open at all times.
-- src:82 | (2) All other instruments shall be signed:
-- src:83 | a. By any authorized officer of the corporation; or
-- src:84 | b. If it shall appear from the instrument that there are no such officers, then by a majority of the directors or by such directors as may be designated by the board; or
-- src:85 | c. If it shall appear from the instrument that there are no such officers or directors, then by the holders of record, or such of them as may be designated by the holders of record, of a majority of all outstanding shares of stock; or
-- src:86 | d. By the holders of record of all outstanding shares of stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(a)(2) (src:82-86)
GIVEN s IS A `s 103(a)(2) Signing for the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(a)(2) the instrument is signed as required for the corporation` s MEANS
        s's `an authorized officer of the corporation signed`
     OR (    s's `it appears from the instrument that there are no such officers`
         AND (   s's `a majority of the directors signed`
              OR s's `such directors as the board designated signed`))
     OR (    s's `it appears from the instrument that there are no such officers or directors`
         AND (   s's `the holders of record of a majority of all outstanding shares of stock signed`
              OR s's `such of the holders of record as the holders of a majority of all outstanding shares designated signed`))
     OR s's `the holders of record of all outstanding shares of stock signed`

-- src:80 | (a) Whenever any instrument is to be filed with the Secretary of State or in accordance with this section or chapter, such instrument shall be executed as follows:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(a) (src:80-86)
GIVEN i IS A `s 103(a) Instrument`
      incorporators IS A `s 103(a)(1) Signing by the incorporators`
      corporation IS A `s 103(a)(2) Signing for the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(a) the instrument is executed as required` i incorporators corporation MEANS
    IF `s 103(a)(1) the instrument is one that the incorporators sign` i
    THEN `s 103(a)(1) the instrument is signed as required of the incorporators` i incorporators
    ELSE `s 103(a)(2) the instrument is signed as required for the corporation` corporation

§§ `s 103(b) Acknowledgment`

-- src:87 | (b) Whenever this chapter requires any instrument to be acknowledged, such requirement is satisfied by either:
-- src:88 | (1) The formal acknowledgment by the person or 1 of the persons signing the instrument that it is such person’s act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation, and that the facts stated therein are true. Such acknowledgment shall be made before a person who is authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds. If such person has a seal of …
-- src:89 | (2) The signature, without more, of the person or persons signing the instrument, in which case such signature or signatures shall constitute the affirmation or acknowledgment of the signatory, under penalties of perjury, that the instrument is such person’s act …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(b) (src:87-89)
DECLARE `s 103(b) Acknowledgment` HAS
    `the instrument was signed`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person signing acknowledged that the instrument is that person's act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation and that the facts stated in it are true` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acknowledgment was made before a person authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person has a seal of office`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person affixed the seal of office to the instrument`                                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:88 | (1) The formal acknowledgment by the person or 1 of the persons signing the instrument that it is such person’s act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation, and that the facts stated therein are true. Such acknowledgment shall be made before a person who is authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds. If such person has a seal of …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(b)(1) (src:88)
GIVEN a IS A `s 103(b) Acknowledgment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(b)(1) the formal acknowledgment has been made` a MEANS
        a's `a person signing acknowledged that the instrument is that person's act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation and that the facts stated in it are true`
    AND a's `the acknowledgment was made before a person authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds`
    AND (   NOT (a's `that person has a seal of office`)
         OR a's `that person affixed the seal of office to the instrument`)

-- The signature "without more" is itself the acknowledgment (it is not a second act).
-- src:89 | (2) The signature, without more, of the person or persons signing the instrument, in which case such signature or signatures shall constitute the affirmation or acknowledgment of the signatory, under penalties of perjury, that the instrument is such person’s act …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(b)(2) (src:89)
GIVEN a IS A `s 103(b) Acknowledgment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(b)(2) the signature alone is the acknowledgment` a MEANS
    a's `the instrument was signed`

-- src:87 | (b) Whenever this chapter requires any instrument to be acknowledged, such requirement is satisfied by either:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(b) (src:87-89)
GIVEN a IS A `s 103(b) Acknowledgment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(b) the requirement that the instrument be acknowledged is satisfied` a MEANS
        `s 103(b)(1) the formal acknowledgment has been made` a
     OR `s 103(b)(2) the signature alone is the acknowledgment` a

-- A signatory who relies on the signature alone affirms, under penalties of perjury, the matters the text lists.
-- src:89 | (2) The signature, without more, of the person or persons signing the instrument, in which case such signature or signatures shall constitute the affirmation or acknowledgment of the signatory, under penalties of perjury, that the instrument is such person’s act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation, and that the facts stated therein shall be true at the time such instrument becomes effective in accordance with this …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(b)(2) (src:89)
GIVEN a IS A `s 103(b) Acknowledgment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(b)(2) the signatory affirms under penalties of perjury that the facts stated are true` a MEANS
        `s 103(b)(2) the signature alone is the acknowledgment` a
    AND (NOT (`s 103(b)(1) the formal acknowledgment has been made` a))

§§ `s 103(c) Filing`

-- src:90 | (c) Whenever any instrument is to be filed with the Secretary of State or in accordance with this section or chapter, such requirement means that:
-- src:91 | (1) The signed instrument shall be delivered to the office of the Secretary of State;
-- src:92 | (2) All taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing of the instrument shall be tendered to the Secretary of State; and
-- src:93 | (3) Upon delivery of the instrument, the Secretary of State shall record the date and time of its delivery. Upon such delivery and tender of the required taxes and fees, …
-- src:94 | (4) Upon request made upon or prior to delivery, the Secretary of State may, to the extent deemed practicable, establish as the filing date of an instrument a date and …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c) (src:90-94)
DECLARE `s 103(c) Steps of filing` HAS
    `the signed instrument was delivered to the office of the Secretary of State`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `all taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing were tendered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State refused to file the instrument due to an error, omission or other imperfection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State endorsed the signed instrument with the word Filed and the date and time of its filing` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:91 | (1) The signed instrument shall be delivered to the office of the Secretary of State;
-- src:92 | (2) All taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing of the instrument shall be tendered to the Secretary of State; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(1), (2) (src:91-92)
