    AND f's `all taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing were tendered`

-- Upon delivery and tender the Secretary of State "shall certify" that the instrument has been filed. The
-- Secretary of State may instead refuse for an error, omission or other imperfection (paragraph (c)(4)); that
-- judgment is the Secretary of State's and is taken as an input.
