-- "The Secretary of State shall not issue a certificate of good standing with respect to any corporation with an
-- instrument held in suspension." Other conditions for a certificate of good standing are not in this section.
-- src:94 | the required taxes and fees within 5 business days after notice of such suspension is given to the filer, the Secretary of State shall establish as the filing date of such instrument the date and …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(4) (src:94)
GIVEN `an instrument of the corporation is held in suspension under paragraph (c)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(c)(4) the Secretary of State is barred from issuing a certificate of good standing` `an instrument of the corporation is held in suspension under paragraph (c)(4)` MEANS
    `an instrument of the corporation is held in suspension under paragraph (c)(4)`

-- The filing date. Except as paragraph (c)(4) and subsection (i) provide, it is the date of delivery.
-- src:93 | actual fraud. The Secretary of State shall file and index the endorsed instrument. Except as provided in paragraph (c)(4) of this section and in subsection (i) of this section, such filing date of an instrument shall be the date and …
-- src:94 | (4) Upon request made upon or prior to delivery, the Secretary of State may, to the extent deemed practicable, establish as the filing date of an instrument a date and time after its delivery. If the Secretary of State refuses to file any instrument due …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(3), (4) (src:93-94)
DECLARE `s 103(c) Route to the filing date` IS ONE OF
    `the date of delivery`
    `a later date established on request made on or before delivery`
        HAS `the later date the Secretary of State established` IS A DATE
    `replacement of an instrument held in suspension`
        HAS `the filing date the rejected instrument would have had if accepted` IS A DATE
            `the number of business days from notice of the suspension to delivery of the replacement` IS A NUMBER
            `the replacement was in proper form and the required taxes and fees were tendered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the information under paragraph (c)(8)`
        HAS `the date on which the information was entered` IS A DATE
            `the number of hours from entry of the information to delivery` IS A NUMBER
            `the instrument was delivered on the date on which the information was entered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an earlier date established under subsection (i)`
        HAS `the earlier date the Secretary of State established under subsection (i)` IS A DATE

-- A route whose conditions are not met does not apply, and the filing date is then the date of delivery.
-- Replacement: within 5 business days after notice (the fifth day is inside). Entry of the information: the
-- same date and within 4 hours after the entry (the fourth hour is inside). Both limits are read as inclusive.
-- src:93 | actual fraud. The Secretary of State shall file and index the endorsed instrument. Except as provided in paragraph (c)(4) of this section and in subsection (i) of this section, such filing date of an instrument shall be the date and …
-- src:94 | (4) Upon request made upon or prior to delivery, the Secretary of State may, to the extent deemed practicable, establish as the filing date of an instrument a date and time after its delivery. If the Secretary of State refuses to file any instrument due …
-- src:94 | issue a certificate of good standing with respect to any corporation with an instrument held in suspension pursuant to this subsection. The Secretary of State may establish as the filing date of an instrument the date and time at which information from such instrument is entered pursuant to paragraph (c)(8) of this section if such instrument is delivered on the …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(3), (4) (src:93-94)
GIVEN route IS A `s 103(c) Route to the filing date`
      `the date of delivery of the instrument` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 103(c)(3) the filing date of the instrument` route `the date of delivery of the instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `the date of delivery` THEN `the date of delivery of the instrument`
    WHEN `a later date established on request made on or before delivery` later THEN later
    WHEN `replacement of an instrument held in suspension` rejected days proper THEN
        IF proper AND (days AT LEAST 0) AND (days AT MOST 5)
        THEN rejected
        ELSE `the date of delivery of the instrument`
    WHEN `entry of the information under paragraph (c)(8)` entered hours same THEN
        IF same AND (hours AT LEAST 0) AND (hours AT MOST 4)
        THEN entered
        ELSE `the date of delivery of the instrument`
    WHEN `an earlier date established under subsection (i)` earlier THEN earlier

-- Paragraphs (c)(5) to (7): the assessment fee for the counties, the Secretary of State's 1 percent
-- administrative charge, and the courthouse municipality fee. The amounts are in dollars.
-- src:95 | (5) The Secretary of State, acting as agent for the recorders of each of the counties, shall collect and deposit in a separate account established …
-- src:95 | assessment fees, the Secretary of State shall retain and pay over to the General Fund of the State an administrative charge of 1 percent of the total fees collected.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(5) (src:95)
GIVEN `the total county assessment fees collected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 103(c)(5) the administrative charge the Secretary of State retains and pays to the General Fund` `the total county assessment fees collected` MEANS
    (`the total county assessment fees collected` TIMES 1%)

-- src:96 | (6) The assessment fee to the counties shall be $24 for each 1-page instrument filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with this section and $9.00 for each additional …
-- src:96 | additional page for instruments with more than 1 page. The recorder’s office to receive the assessment fee shall be the recorder’s office in the county in which the corporation’s registered office in this State is, or is to be, located, except that an assessment fee shall not be charged for either a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b. of this title or a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI of this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(6) (src:96)
GIVEN pages IS A NUMBER
      `the instrument is a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b.` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 103(c)(6) the county assessment fee` pages `the instrument is a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b.` `the instrument is a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI` MEANS
    -- out of range: section 391(a)(5)b. (piece dg11) and subchapter XVI (piece dg10), taken as facts.
    IF (pages LESS THAN 1) OR (NOT (FLOOR pages EQUALS pages))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the instrument is a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b.` OR `the instrument is a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE JUST (24 PLUS (9 TIMES (pages MINUS 1)))

-- src:96 | additional page for instruments with more than 1 page. The recorder’s office to receive the assessment fee shall be the recorder’s office in the county in which the corporation’s registered office in this State is, or is to be, located, except that an assessment fee shall not be charged for either a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b. of this title or a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI of this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(6) (src:96)
GIVEN `the county in which the corporation's registered office in this State is, or is to be, located` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 103(c)(6) the county whose recorder's office receives the assessment fee` `the county in which the corporation's registered office in this State is, or is to be, located` MEANS
    `the county in which the corporation's registered office in this State is, or is to be, located`

-- src:97 | with the Secretary of State in accordance with this section. The municipality to receive the fee shall be the municipality designated in § 301 of Title 10 in the county in which the corporation’s registered office in this State is, or is to be, located, except that a fee shall not be charged for a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b. of this title, a resignation of agent without appointment of a successor under § 136 of this title, or a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI of this …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(c)(7) (src:97)
GIVEN `the instrument is a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b.` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a resignation of agent without appointment of a successor under § 136` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 103(c)(7) the courthouse municipality fee` `the instrument is a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b.` `the instrument is a resignation of agent without appointment of a successor under § 136` `the instrument is a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI` MEANS
    -- out of range: sections 136 (piece dg2), 391(a)(5)b. (piece dg11) and subchapter XVI (piece dg10), taken as facts.
    IF    `the instrument is a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under § 391(a)(5)b.`
       OR `the instrument is a resignation of agent without appointment of a successor under § 136`
       OR `the instrument is a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 40

