-- "Extraordinary condition" means, in the first limb, an emergency resulting from an event of the first two
-- kinds in the United States or a locality described, or the immediate threat of one; in the second limb, a
-- malfunction or outage, or weather or other condition, as a result of which the Secretary of State's office is
-- not open for filing or filing cannot be effected without extraordinary effort. The definition is exhaustive.
-- src:109 | (2) For purposes of this subsection, an “extraordinary condition” means: any emergency resulting from an attack on, invasion or occupation by foreign military forces of, or disaster, catastrophe, war or other armed conflict, revolution or insurrection, or rioting or civil commotion in, the United States or a locality in which the Secretary of State conducts its business or in which the good faith effort to deliver the instrument and tender the required taxes and fees is made, or the immediate threat of any of the foregoing; or any malfunction or outage of the electrical or telephone service to the Secretary of State’s office, or weather or other condition in or about a locality in which the Secretary of State conducts its business, as a result of which the Secretary of State’s office is not open for the purpose of the filing of instruments under this chapter or such filing cannot be effected without extraordinary effort. The Secretary of State may require such proof as it deems necessary to make the determination required under paragraph (i)(1)c. of this section, and any such determination shall be conclusive in the absence of actual fraud.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(i)(2) (src:109)
GIVEN event IS A `s 103(i)(2) Event`
      place IS A `s 103(i)(2) Place`
      `it is an emergency resulting from the event, or the immediate threat of the event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office of the Secretary of State is not open for the purpose of the filing of instruments under this chapter, or the filing cannot be effected without extraordinary effort` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(i)(2) there is an extraordinary condition` event place `it is an emergency resulting from the event, or the immediate threat of the event` `the office of the Secretary of State is not open for the purpose of the filing of instruments under this chapter, or the filing cannot be effected without extraordinary effort` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `an attack on, or invasion or occupation by foreign military forces of` THEN
        `it is an emergency resulting from the event, or the immediate threat of the event` AND (NOT (place EQUALS `another place`))
    WHEN `a disaster, catastrophe, war or other armed conflict, revolution or insurrection, or rioting or civil commotion in` THEN
        `it is an emergency resulting from the event, or the immediate threat of the event` AND (NOT (place EQUALS `another place`))
    WHEN `a malfunction or outage of the electrical or telephone service to the office of the Secretary of State` THEN
        `the office of the Secretary of State is not open for the purpose of the filing of instruments under this chapter, or the filing cannot be effected without extraordinary effort`
    WHEN `weather or other condition in or about a locality in which the Secretary of State conducts its business` THEN
        `the office of the Secretary of State is not open for the purpose of the filing of instruments under this chapter, or the filing cannot be effected without extraordinary effort`
    WHEN `another event` THEN FALSE

-- The Secretary of State may require proof; the determination is conclusive in the absence of actual fraud.
-- src:109 | conducts its business, as a result of which the Secretary of State’s office is not open for the purpose of the filing of instruments under this chapter or such filing cannot be effected without extraordinary effort. The Secretary of State may require such proof as it deems necessary to make the determination required under paragraph (i)(1)c. of this section, and any such determination shall be conclusive in the absence of actual …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 103(i)(2) (src:109)
GIVEN `there was actual fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 103(i)(2) the determination of the Secretary of State is conclusive` `there was actual fraud` MEANS
    NOT (`there was actual fraud`)

